WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.676
Module 1: licenses, programs and waves.

00:00:02.676 --> 00:00:07.067
In the Mosaic course you learned
the four ways into Culture Dig.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.361
Here you'll learn what
each one actually grants,

00:00:10.361 --> 00:00:15.850
so you can tell a client exactly what
they're buying, who can buy the next wave,

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:19.692
and what happens to their
program if a license runs out.

00:00:19.692 --> 00:00:21.133
About thirty minutes.

00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:23.992
However a client gets Culture Dig,

00:00:23.992 --> 00:00:28.224
they get the same right: to run
programs in one organization.

00:00:28.224 --> 00:00:31.416
Two things on the license
make the difference.

00:00:31.416 --> 00:00:35.301
The source says how it was
sold: issued by Mosaic staff,

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:39.047
bought as a licensee add-on,
or bought on the website.

00:00:39.047 --> 00:00:43.626
And the program allowance says how
many programs the money bought.

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:47.095
If there's no number at
all, that means unlimited.

00:00:47.095 --> 00:00:50.980
Culture Dig is priced per
program, never per respondent,

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:55.629
so the allowance is what stops one
purchase becoming many programs.

00:00:55.629 --> 00:01:00.901
When it's used up, the hub says so
plainly: this license covers one program,

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.358
and it has been used.

00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:04.374
Let's walk the table.

00:01:04.374 --> 00:01:07.748
When the Mosaic team runs
the dig and invoices,

00:01:07.748 --> 00:01:12.485
staff issue a license with no
program limit and no per-wave limit.

00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:17.223
A website purchase adds one program,
with its first wave included,

00:01:17.223 --> 00:01:21.027
and later waves are bought
one at a time, up to four.

00:01:21.027 --> 00:01:25.047
The licensee add-on comes in
two shapes: per engagement,

00:01:25.047 --> 00:01:28.564
which works like the
website purchase, or annual,

00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:32.082
which is unlimited programs
and waves for a year.

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:34.091
It doesn't renew on its own.

00:01:34.091 --> 00:01:39.906
Only organizations with a live SurveyCraft
platform license can buy either shape.

00:01:39.906 --> 00:01:44.069
Coaches can also launch a dig
from Mosaic Coaching Studio,

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:48.591
in an organization of its own:
a paid launch includes one wave,

00:01:48.591 --> 00:01:51.821
and an included launch
has no per-wave limit.

00:01:51.821 --> 00:01:57.133
And whichever route, a website purchase
is the software, not facilitation.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:01.799
Prices change, so check the current
price sheet before you quote.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.641
Four rules decide what
a second purchase does.

00:02:05.641 --> 00:02:10.870
A purchase adds to the allowance, it
never replaces it: one becomes two.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.485
A purchase revives a lapsed license,

00:02:13.485 --> 00:02:16.971
so someone who pays again
isn't left locked out.

00:02:16.971 --> 00:02:22.490
Unlimited swallows everything: an annual
license replaces the allowance with

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:28.301
unlimited, and the checkout won't sell
unlimited to an organization that already

00:02:28.301 --> 00:02:28.809
has it.

00:02:28.809 --> 00:02:33.820
And a per-engagement purchase never
shortens a year already paid for.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:39.413
So when a client asks whether they need
to buy anything to start another dig,

00:02:39.413 --> 00:02:41.301
look at the license first.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.512
Here's a practice decision.

00:02:43.512 --> 00:02:48.268
A partner that holds a platform license
expects to run five digs this year.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.107
Which add-on should they buy?

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.124
Three different things happen to
a wave, and clients mix them up.

00:02:55.124 --> 00:03:00.692
A wave is included when the program has
paid for it; the program page says "This

00:03:00.692 --> 00:03:03.198
program includes one of four waves".

00:03:03.198 --> 00:03:06.122
It's added when someone buys the next one.

00:03:06.122 --> 00:03:11.272
And it's started when the program moves
to it: teams get fresh workspaces,

00:03:11.272 --> 00:03:15.657
and the story link waits for
prompts approved for the new wave.

00:03:15.657 --> 00:03:20.251
Starting can be undone, and nothing
from the last wave is touched.

00:03:20.251 --> 00:03:23.940
You can only buy the next
wave, never one further on.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:27.699
Programs under an invoiced
license, an annual license,

00:03:27.699 --> 00:03:31.457
or an included coaching launch
have no per-wave limit.

00:03:31.457 --> 00:03:37.234
And an annual license bought later lifts
the limit on programs that were bought one

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:38.278
at a time, too.

00:03:38.278 --> 00:03:44.125
Northwind's program includes one wave, so
wave two will need adding before November.

00:03:44.633 --> 00:03:47.845
Buying a wave spends the
organization's money.

00:03:47.845 --> 00:03:53.502
So the person who presses Add wave must
be a Program Lead who is also an admin of

00:03:53.502 --> 00:03:54.689
the organization.

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:58.878
An outside consultant made lead
is told an admin can add it.

00:03:58.878 --> 00:04:04.255
At Northwind, that's only Alex, because
Jamie, the second lead, is an editor.

00:04:04.255 --> 00:04:06.350
As the Facilitator, you can't.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.841
Name who will buy wave two
when you plan wave one.

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:14.497
A license gates the running
program, not just its creation.

00:04:14.497 --> 00:04:20.002
If it lapses, every program goes read-only:
no new fieldwork, no report edits,

00:04:20.002 --> 00:04:20.849
no analysis.

00:04:20.849 --> 00:04:26.213
The public story link closes, and
respondents simply see that it isn't open.

00:04:26.213 --> 00:04:27.625
But nothing is lost.

00:04:27.625 --> 00:04:31.295
Findings, stories and reports
can all still be read.

00:04:31.295 --> 00:04:35.388
The organization's owners and
admins, and the Mosaic team,

00:04:35.388 --> 00:04:39.129
are warned at thirty days,
seven days and on the day.

00:04:39.129 --> 00:04:44.634
Website and per-engagement purchases
don't expire, but an annual license does.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:47.810
If it ends in the middle
of story collection,

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:51.339
a whole workforce is shut
out with no explanation.

00:04:51.339 --> 00:04:53.879
Check the term before you set dates.

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:58.171
Three ways to end a program,
and they're very different.

00:04:58.171 --> 00:05:01.296
Mark program complete is
for the Program Lead.

00:05:01.296 --> 00:05:06.051
It closes the story link, and reopening
the program doesn't reopen it.

00:05:06.051 --> 00:05:11.486
Archive is for the organization's owners
and admins: the program goes read-only,

00:05:11.486 --> 00:05:15.562
the link shows it has ended,
and Restore brings it all back.

00:05:15.562 --> 00:05:18.007
It still counts against the license.

00:05:18.007 --> 00:05:19.366
Delete is permanent.

00:05:19.366 --> 00:05:23.306
It removes everything, including
every story people wrote.

00:05:23.306 --> 00:05:26.363
And if the program
collected anything at all,

00:05:26.363 --> 00:05:30.032
it still counts against the
allowance after it's gone.

00:05:30.032 --> 00:05:35.194
So deleting a dig that ran buys nothing
back; it just destroys the evidence.

00:05:35.194 --> 00:05:39.678
Between waves, don't mark a program
complete just to stop stories.

00:05:39.678 --> 00:05:42.667
Use Close collection,
which you can reverse.

00:05:43.167 --> 00:05:44.857
One more practice decision.

00:05:44.857 --> 00:05:50.117
Suppose someone created a test program by
accident, and now the real one is refused.

00:05:50.117 --> 00:05:51.369
What should they do?

00:05:51.867 --> 00:05:55.961
Time for the module check: six
questions, and you need five right.

00:05:55.961 --> 00:05:57.326
Retakes are unlimited.

00:05:57.833 --> 00:06:02.538
Here's your License and Wave Decision
Card: what the client holds,

00:06:02.538 --> 00:06:06.957
starting a program, starting a
wave, and pausing or finishing.

00:06:06.957 --> 00:06:07.812
Download it.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:09.065
To sum up.

00:06:09.065 --> 00:06:12.127
A license's source says how it was sold,

00:06:12.127 --> 00:06:15.877
and its allowance says
how many programs it buys.

00:06:15.877 --> 00:06:19.856
Purchases add up, and
unlimited swallows everything.

00:06:19.856 --> 00:06:25.443
Waves are included, added by a lead
who's also an org admin, and started.

00:06:25.443 --> 00:06:30.648
A lapsed license means read-only
and a closed link, never lost data.

00:06:30.648 --> 00:06:34.551
And close collection to
pause, archive to put away,

00:06:34.551 --> 00:06:37.536
and delete only what collected nothing.

00:06:37.536 --> 00:06:39.908
Next: people, roles and access.
